<#
.SYNOPSIS
    FirstBase Audit Mode update progress UI.
    For Internal Use Only.

.DESCRIPTION
    Fullscreen WPF splash (borderless maximized + strongest practical topmost
    stack: WPF Topmost + Win32 HWND_TOPMOST / WS_EX_TOPMOST + existing 2213z/2214*
    tick). Tails the most recent
    C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase\Logs\WU-*.log and parses it for current pass /
    KB ID / install activity.

    2309-splash-above-oobe-os-limitation (superseded in part by 5.4.5):
      - Reliably *activating* this splash above Win11 OOBE without tech input is
        still an OS limitation. 5.4.5 hides OOBE hosts with ``SW_HIDE`` (not
        ``SW_MINIMIZE``) when splash is confirmed visible and the WU loop is
        painting over Audit (5.4.19 will not hide CXH as the only UI). 5.4.20
        re-asserts SW_HIDE each splash tick (language/keyboard/region and the
        CXH "problem getting this PC ready" error) while painting; seal restores
        customer OOBE. OOBE is
        blacked out behind the existing Topmost fullscreen splash. ``SW_MINIMIZE``
        on WWAHost CoreWindow is the 2214j trap (black layer *above* splash) and
        stays opt-in via ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_FORCE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE``. Layer 2 kill
        remains default OFF. Seal-window / ``.firstbase-sealed`` / Updates-Done
        teardown restore OOBE. Opt out: ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_DISABLE_OOBE_HIDE=1``.

    2300-splash-oobe-suppression-layers:
      - Layered, independently-toggleable OOBE-suppression so the update splash reliably surfaces on every audit-phase
        boot (root-caused: an OOBE host - usually WWAHost/CoreWindow - holds the foreground lock, so SetForegroundWindow
        is denied until recent input, i.e. the "only works after Shift+F10" symptom). All mechanisms are wrapped in
        try/catch (can never crash the splash), instrumented for field bisection, and honor a single seal-window guard so
        they neutralize themselves the moment the loop begins sysprep hand-off (real customer OOBE is regenerated by
        sysprep /oobe and must stay intact).
      - Phase 0 (diagnostics, ALWAYS ON): ``Write-SplashSuppressionLog`` -> dedicated ``splash-oobe-suppression.log`` and a
        central ``Get-FbSplashSuppressionConfig`` that reads env vars first, then the config file
        ``C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase\splash-suppression.cfg`` (dropped by SetupComplete.cmd) so a field tech can flip a
        layer without a rebuild. Global kill switch: ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_SUPPRESSION_DISABLE=1``. ``-SimulateOobeForeground``
        preview/test hook spawns a dummy topmost window so the reclaim/kill logic can be exercised off-hardware.
      - Layer 1 fglock (``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_FGLOCK``, default ON): ``SystemParametersInfo(SPI_SETFOREGROUNDLOCKTIMEOUT, 0)``
        at startup so the reclaim/2296 path succeeds every tick (SetupComplete also seeds HKCU ForegroundLockTimeout=0).
      - Layer 2 killoobe (``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_KILL_OOBE``, default OFF): when an OOBE-family host is foreground, the refresh
        timer ``Stop-Process -Force`` it (NEVER minimize the WWAHost CoreWindow - that caused the 2214g/2214h black screen)
        with a per-boot kill counter + backoff; halted by the seal-window guard regardless of toggle.
      - Layer 3 shell (``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_SHELL``, default OFF): most invasive; SetupComplete swaps Winlogon Shell to
        FirstBaseSplashShell.cmd for the audit session (see SetupComplete.cmd / FirstBaseSplashWatcher.ps1); reverted to
        explorer.exe before seal.
      - Layer 4 oobeflags (``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_OOBE_FLAGS``, default OFF): audit-only OOBE setup-state suppression flags;
        sysprep /oobe re-arms real OOBE for the customer. Set/reverted from the loop, gated by the seal-window guard.

    2296-splash-oobe-synth-input-fg-reclaim:
      - OOBE's foreground lock frequently denies ``SetForegroundWindow`` during the 2214a/2214b reclaim because no
        recent input has occurred - the same reason a manual **Shift+F10** (opening a console) is what makes the splash
        pop to the front. Fires a harmless synthetic **VK_F15** key down+up (``keybd_event`` via ``FbSplashWin32Z``)
        IMMEDIATELY BEFORE the reclaim ``SetForegroundWindow`` so Windows treats the change as input-driven and honors it,
        emulating the Shift+F10 effect without a tech touching the keyboard.
      - Runs on the **gated** reclaim path only (foreground is an OOBE host and we are actually reclaiming), and once in
        ``Invoke-FbSplashTryForegroundOnce`` before its one-time ``SetForegroundWindow`` - **not** unconditionally per tick.
      - **VK_F15** is inert in OOBE so it does not perturb the OOBE UI. Default **ON**; env
        ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_DISABLE_SYNTH_INPUT=1`` opts out. All native calls are wrapped so a failure can never crash the splash.

    2026.05.13.2213c-onlogon-primary-and-defender-disable UX pivot (superseded
    for OOBE dominance by 2221 below - chrome removed again on purpose):
      - WindowStyle=SingleBorderWindow (thin chrome with min/max/close).
      - WindowState=Maximized (covers the screen but is windowed).
      - ResizeMode=CanResize so the tech can resize manually.
      - ShowInTaskbar=True so the window shows up in Alt+Tab / taskbar.

    2026.05.22.2221-splash-borderless-max-oobe-visibility:
      - WindowStyle=None + WindowState=Maximized + ResizeMode=NoResize + Topmost=True
        + ShowInTaskbar=True (taskbar/Alt+Tab visibility for tech debuggability on
        audit-mode consoles; OOBE may still hide taskbar - document only).
      - WindowStartupLocation=CenterScreen so the maximized root lands on a
        sensible monitor in multi-display setups before covering that screen.
      - 2218 handoff: when FirstBase-Updates-Done.flag exists AND
        FirstBase-Splash-Oobe-Overlay.mode exists, defer closing and switch copy to
        "awaiting sysprep/reboot" until the overlay marker disappears.
      - 2026.05.22.2222-handoff-oobe-zorder: while that handoff is active (both files),
        2214l/2214e stay enabled; 2214c skips the per-tick "marker-present" restore that
        otherwise popped WWAHost above the splash (fb-dump-final-1332).

    2026.05.20.2213u-splash-topmost-oobe-safe (user-approved unfreeze):
      - Topmost=True by default; Loaded + 2.5s timer refresh WPF Topmost
        + Activate() (F12 can opt out).

    2026.05.20.2213z-splash-hwnd-topmost-oobe (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1143):
      - OOBE / oobeldr often sits above WPF Topmost alone. After
        SourceInitialized, cache HwndSource.Handle and call Win32
        SetWindowPos(..., HWND_TOPMOST, SWP_NOMOVE|SWP_NOSIZE|SWP_SHOWWINDOW)
        alongside the existing WPF Topmost + Activate path on Loaded and on
        the same 2.5s timer (still gated by UserPreferredTopmostOff / F12).
      - F12 OFF applies HWND_NOTOPMOST so native z-order matches intent.
      - Loaded: one-time AllowSetForegroundWindow(ASFW_ANY) +
        SetForegroundWindow(hwnd) for initial visibility (can briefly steal
        focus from OOBE; product-approved for tech visibility during updates).
      - F12 still toggles Topmost + native topmost with the brief on-screen
        "Always-on-top: ON / OFF" indicator (2s fade-out).
      - Esc still minimizes the window.
      - Window close (Alt+F4 / X button) is STILL blocked until the
        Marker file appears - preserves the prior invariant that a
        tech cannot accidentally dismiss the dashboard while updates
        are still running.

    2026.05.20.2214a-splash-exstyle-oobe-fg-reclaim (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1218):
      - 2213z still lost z-order vs OOBE on some builds. Adds Win32
        GWL_EXSTYLE WS_EX_TOPMOST (SetWindowLongPtr) alongside SetWindowPos
        when fighting for top; cleared when F12 turns topmost off.
      - Same 2.5s timer: if foreground HWND belongs to oobeldr /
        UserOOBEBroker / CloudExperienceHost, re-issue AllowSetForegroundWindow
        + SetForegroundWindow and log fg proc/class to splash-ui.log (2214a).

    2026.05.20.2214b-splash-oobe-attach-fg (Win11 25H2 OOBE region page):
      - OOBE can keep splash visible (topmost) but block focus; 2214a reclaim
        often failed SetForegroundWindow without input-attachment. Before
        SetForegroundWindow on splash, AttachThreadInput(foreground thread,
        current dispatcher thread), detach in finally; log 2214b lines.
      - ShellExperienceHost.exe included in OOBE foreground reclaim set.
      - Optional BringWindowToTop after reclaim SetForegroundWindow.

    2026.05.20.2214c-splash-oobe-minimize-while-updates (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1314):
      - OOBE can still paint above splash / console fallback on 25H2; 2214b
        AttachThreadInput-FG was not enough for a clean visual stack.
      - While FirstBase-Updates-Done.flag is absent and F12 has not disabled
        topmost: enumerate visible top-level HWNDs owned by oobeldr /
        UserOOBEBroker / CloudExperienceHost / ShellExperienceHost (excluding
        the splash HWND), ShowWindow(SW_MINIMIZE), track for restore.
      - Restore ShowWindow(SW_RESTORE) when the marker appears, on splash
        close, or when F12 turns always-on-top off. Every hide/restore logs
        to splash-ui.log with tag ``2214c`` + HWND + proc + reason.
      - 2214b foreground reclaim + 2213z topmost stack remain (minimize runs
        first in the 2.5s tick so OOBE is off-screen before z-order/focus work).

    2026.05.20.2214k-splash-visibility-extra-diag:
      - Throttled ``2214k: TopmostTick-extras`` in ``splash-ui.log``: splash ``GWL_EXSTYLE``,
        ``IsWindowVisible`` / ``IsIconic``, WPF ``Topmost`` / ``IsActive``, foreground-root
        vis/iconic, and up to 5 ``GetWindow(GW_HWNDPREV)`` Z-order steps above the splash HWND.

    2026.05.20.2214l-splash-oobe-zbehind-splash:
      - When OOBE foreground is **WWAHost.exe** ``Windows.UI.Core.CoreWindow`` (2214j skip family),
        **SetWindowPos** places the OOBE **GA_ROOT** HWND **immediately below** the splash HWND
        (``hwndInsertAfter`` = splash; ``SWP_NOMOVE|SWP_NOSIZE|SWP_NOACTIVATE``; **no** ``SWP_NOZORDER``),
        throttled **4s** per root HWND. Logs ``2214l: OOBE-Z-behind-splash ...``. Runs only while
        updates marker absent, F12 topmost on, after splash **HWND_TOPMOST** restack  -  **no**
        ``SW_FORCEMINIMIZE`` / ``HWND_NOTOPMOST`` on OOBE (2214h).

    2026.05.22.2224-splash-layout-oobe:
      - Removed splash **Version** / payload footnote block for more list vertical space; taller updates list (720p-friendly).
      - Row status icons use ASCII-only (avoid odd glyphs in some fonts); activity lines strip ``%`` (percent removed from install/download UI text at loop source; display sanitizer is backup).
      - 2221 overlay handoff: optional throttled extra native **Topmost** + **2214l** refresh on the **main** handoff timer (``2224f`` log). **2214j** WWAHost fg-root skip remains default; **2226** env ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_FORCE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE=1`` enables one override path (WARN).

    2026.05.22.2225-splash-replace-fix (fb-dump-final-1520):
      - ``Remove-FbSplashPercentFromDisplayText``: PowerShell ``-replace`` accepts only **two** operands; removed invalid third argument (``'IgnoreCase'``) - use ``(?i)`` inline regex flag so ``ShowDialog()`` no longer throws on first UI tick.

    2026.05.20.2214n-splash-minimal-ui-usb-logs:
      - Replace verbose ``Phase: ...`` line with one short status string; cap ``message`` / log-derived activity length for display.

    Centralized versioning (``Payload\FirstBaseVersion.ps1`` + ``FirstBaseVersion.cmd``):
      - Product / payload / per-script semver are single-sourced; splash reads display version from manifest.

    2026.05.20.2214m-splash-oobe-zbehind-hardened:
      - **2214l** follow-up: ``SetLastError(0)`` before ``SetWindowPos`` (via ``FbSplashWin32Z``), log
        ``gle=`` from ``GetLastError``/``Marshal.GetLastWin32Error`` on every Z-stomp attempt; **two**
        ``SetWindowPos`` passes in the same **1.5s** tick when pass **1** ran (**pass=1** after topmost,
        **pass=2** after **2214b** reclaim  -  shell may re-order Z after foreground work). Throttle **4s**
        applies only to pass **1** per root (pass **2** reuses the same bucket, no extra log cadence).

    2026.05.20.2214j-splash-wwahost-skip-minimize (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1503):
      - ``SW_MINIMIZE`` on ``WWAHost.exe`` / ``Windows.UI.Core.CoreWindow`` returned
        ``ShowWindow=True`` but often left a **black full-screen layer** with splash
        underneath. **2214j:** skip fg-root and 2214c-enum ``SW_MINIMIZE`` for
        ``wwahost.exe``; rely on HWND_TOPMOST + WS_EX_TOPMOST + reclaim. Splash tick
        applies native topmost **before** OOBE minimize (other hosts); interval **1.5s**.

    2026.05.27.2226-wwahost-optional-minimize (lab override):
      - Env ``FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_FORCE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE=1`` enables **one** fg-root ``GA_ROOT``
        ``ShowWindow(SW_MINIMIZE)`` for ``wwahost.exe`` (otherwise skipped by **2214j**). Logs **WARN**
        with black-layer regression note (fb-dump-final-1503). **2214c** enum path still skips WWAHost;
        **2214l** ``SetWindowPos`` gate unchanged (process/class rules not broadened).

    2026.05.20.2214i-splash-launcher-no-console-fallback:
      - ``FirstBaseSplashLauncher.cmd`` no longer runs ``start ... FirstBaseConsoleSplash.cmd``.
        Extra cmd console competed with OOBE/splash focus. WPF-only auto-launch;
        console helper files remain on disk for manual use.

    2026.05.20.2214h-splash-oobe-no-corewindow-aggressive (field regression):
      - **2214g** follow-up ``SW_FORCEMINIMIZE`` + ``SetWindowPos(HWND_NOTOPMOST)``
        on OOBE ``Windows.UI.Core.CoreWindow`` caused a **black full-screen shell**
        while splash only appeared in Alt+Tab until Shift+F10. **2214h:** remove
        those calls; keep ``SW_MINIMIZE`` + ``iconic=`` diag only when ``IsIconic``
        stays false (no further hide on that HWND).

    2026.05.20.2214g-splash-oobe-corewindow-fallback (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1503, superseded by 2214h):
      - Attempted ``SW_FORCEMINIMIZE`` + ``HWND_NOTOPMOST`` when ``SW_MINIMIZE``
        did not set ``IsIconic``  -  **reverted in 2214h** (black screen regression).

    2026.05.20.2214f-splash-oobe-wwahost (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1448):
      - Win11 OOBE region UI often runs in **WWAHost.exe** with class
        ``Windows.UI.Core.CoreWindow`` (diag showed ``oobePidCount=0`` because
        no CloudExperienceHost/ApplicationFrameHost PIDs; FG was WWAHost).
      - Add ``WWAHost`` to PID enum + foreground-root minimize + 2214b reclaim.

    2026.05.20.2214e-splash-oobe-pidlist-fgroot-minimize (field: F:\\fb-dump-final-1434):
      - 2214d tick diag threw ``Count`` on ``$pids.Count`` because PowerShell
        unwraps a single-element ``List[uint32]`` return to a scalar; the
        same bug hit ``Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214cApplyMinimizeWhileUpdates`` inside
        ``catch {}``, silencing ALL 2214c enum minimizes. Fix: return PID list
        as ``[pscustomobject]@{ PidList = $list }``; defensive ``$hits`` length.
      - Foreground OOBE suppress (2214e): minimize ``GetAncestor(fg, GA_ROOT)``
        when foreground proc is ApplicationFrameHost, CloudExperienceHost,
        ShellExperienceHost, UserOOBEBroker, or oobeldr (not splash); log
        ``2214e: OOBE-minimize hide reason=fg-oobe-root``.

    2026.05.20.2218-oobe-sound-deferred-firmware (OOBE overlay only; supersedes 2217 immediate spawn):
    When ``FirstBase-Splash-Oobe-Overlay.mode`` exists, splash exit **does not** open Sound.
    After ``sysprep.exe`` validation exit **0**, ``Invoke-SysprepToOobe`` arms HKLM ``RunOnce``
    ``OpenWindowsSoundSettingsDeferredOnce`` (``FirstBaseDeferredOobeSound.ps1``) and runs
    ``shutdown /r /fw``. Next Windows boot: ``ms-settings:sound`` once, wait for Settings hosts,
    then ``shutdown /s``. See ``Invoke-WindowsUpdateLoop.ps1``.

    Closes when C:\Windows\Setup\Scripts\FirstBase-Updates-Done.flag appears,
    when its scheduled task is killed by SetupComplete cleanup, or when the
    OS reboots (the splash task relaunches it on next boot/logon).

    Lab override: empty file C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase\FirstBase-NoSplash.flag
    suppresses launch (handled in SetupComplete.cmd, not here).
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [switch]$Preview,
    # Off-device preview flavor. Only honored with -Preview:
    #   Static   - sample update list (default; matches the historical preview)
    #   Pulling  - animated check -> download -> install -> done sequence
    #   Checking - empty list / "checking for updates" placeholder state
    [ValidateSet('Static', 'Pulling', 'Checking')]
    [string]$PreviewScenario = 'Static',
    # 2300 Phase 0 test hook: spawn a dummy topmost "OOBE" window so the fg-reclaim / Layer 2 kill logic can be
    # exercised off-hardware in -Preview (no real OOBE host present). Ignored outside -Preview.
    [switch]$SimulateOobeForeground
)

$ErrorActionPreference = 'Continue'
$script:Preview = [bool]$Preview
$script:PreviewScenario = if ($Preview) { $PreviewScenario } else { 'Static' }
$script:SimulateOobeForeground = [bool]$SimulateOobeForeground

# FirstBase wolf logo (256x256 PNG, base64) rendered in the splash header.
$script:FbSplashLogoB64 = ''

$fbVerPs1 = Join-Path 'C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase' 'FirstBaseVersion.ps1'
if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $fbVerPs1)) {
    $fbVerPs1 = Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'FirstBaseVersion.ps1'
}
if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $fbVerPs1) {
    . $fbVerPs1
} else {
    $FirstBaseProductVersion  = '1.0.0'
    $FirstBasePayloadRevision = 'unknown'
    $FirstBaseBuildStatus     = 'release'
    $FirstBaseScriptVersion   = @{}
}
if (-not $FirstBaseBuildStatus) { $FirstBaseBuildStatus = 'release' }
$fbUiLeaf = 'Show-UpdateProgress.ps1'
try {
    if ($MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path) { $fbUiLeaf = Split-Path -Leaf $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path }
} catch {}
$script:ThisScriptVersion = [string]$FirstBaseScriptVersion[$fbUiLeaf]
if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($script:ThisScriptVersion)) { $script:ThisScriptVersion = $FirstBaseProductVersion }
$script:UiVersion = $script:ThisScriptVersion
$script:FbProductDisplayVersion = $FirstBaseProductVersion

$FbRoot = 'C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase'
$LogDir = Join-Path $FbRoot 'Logs'
$Marker = 'C:\Windows\Setup\Scripts\FirstBase-Updates-Done.flag'
# 2218 / 2221: OOBE overlay pipeline marker  -  when present with Updates-Done.flag, splash may defer exit (see main timer).
$FbSplashOobeOverlayMode = 'C:\ProgramData\FirstBase\FirstBase-Splash-Oobe-Overlay.mode'
# 2305: seal-window teardown marker. Invoke-WindowsUpdateLoop.ps1 writes this the moment it opens the OOBE-handoff
# seal window (Invoke-FbOobeHandoff). Once Layer 2 is seal-gated the splash can no longer take the foreground, so
# leaving it up makes it sit BEHIND the real customer OOBE looking broken (field report SD00HN3R 3rd boot). On this
# marker the splash closes + exits so the customer OOBE is clean; FirstBaseSplashWatcher.ps1 stands down on the same
# marker. Path shared with the loop ($FbSealSplashTeardownMarkerPath) and the watcher.
$FbSplashSealTeardownMarker = 'C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase\State\.splash-teardown'
# 5.4.19: WU loop writes this with its PID while painting splash over Audit.
$FbSplashWuLoopPaintingMarker = 'C:\Windows\Setup\FirstBase\State\.wu-loop-painting'
$script:FbSplashLastKnownUpdates = @()
$script:FbSplashTeardownRequested = $false
# 2229: operator finalize wrote this - overlay pipeline complete; stop WWAHost minimize.
$FbSplashPipelineCompletedMarker = 'C:\ProgramData\FirstBase\.pipeline-completed'
# 2295: delivery entered - suppress splash re-fire but overlay pipeline not yet complete.
$FbSplashDeliveryStartedMarker = 'C:\ProgramData\FirstBase\.oobe-sound-delivery-started'
# 2231/2256: operator sealed marker (paired with .pipeline-completed).
$FbSealedMarker = 'C:\ProgramData\FirstBase\.firstbase-sealed'
# 2380 (5.0.39): operator Settings gate active - splash stands down (Topmost off + minimize)
# so the operator's Settings window can take the foreground.
$FbSplashOperatorGateActive = 'C:\ProgramData\FirstBase\.operator-settings-gate-active'
$script:FbSplashOperatorGateStoodDown = $false

function Test-FbSplash2222OobeOverlayHandoffActive {
    # 2222: Updates-done marker is present AND OOBE overlay handoff is still active  -  keep OOBE Z-order
    # mitigation enabled (2214l/2214e/2214c) until scrub removes the overlay file. Without this,
    # marker-only paths restored minimized OOBE and skipped 2214l, leaving handoff copy behind WWAHost.
    # 2256: If operator finalize wrote pipeline/sealed but stale overlay.mode survived, do NOT treat as handoff
    # (fb-dump-final-806 - real-user session stuck on 2221 defer).
    try {
        if ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashPipelineCompletedMarker) -or (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSealedMarker)) {
            return $false
        }
        return ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $Marker) -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashOobeOverlayMode))
    } catch {
        return $false
    }
}

function Test-FbSplash2227OobeOverlayPipelineActive {
    # Overlay.mode is written at STAGE 2 only (after CBS settles), not at specialize.
    # Specialize used to drop this file and Audit splash then SW_MINIMIZE'd Dell
    # WWAHost "Just a moment" for the whole update loop (BWT3CB4-1420).
    # Active when overlay.mode exists (or 2222 handoff), until .pipeline-completed.
    try {
        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashPipelineCompletedMarker) { return $false }
    } catch {}
    try {
        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashOobeOverlayMode) { return $true }
    } catch {}
    return (Test-FbSplash2222OobeOverlayHandoffActive)
}

function Test-FbSplash2227WwahostMinimizeAllowed {
    if ($env:FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_DISABLE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE -eq '1') { return $false }
    # 2241: per-tick gate - skip WWAHost SW_MINIMIZE when splash not yet confirmed visible after 30s.
    if ($script:Fb2241SkipWwahostMinForThisTick) { return $false }
    if (-not (Test-FbSplash2227OobeOverlayPipelineActive)) { return $false }
    if ($env:FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_FORCE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE -eq '1') { return $true }
    # 5.4.5: default OOBE cover is SW_HIDE (see Test-FbSplashOobeHideAllowed), not SW_MINIMIZE.
    return $false
}

function Test-FbSplashWuLoopPaintingActive {
    # 5.4.19: SW_HIDE of WWAHost/CloudExperienceHost is allowed only while the
    # WU loop is live in Audit and splash is the covering UI.
    try {
        if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashWuLoopPaintingMarker)) { return $false }
        $raw = (Get-Content -LiteralPath $FbSplashWuLoopPaintingMarker -ErrorAction Stop | Select-Object -First 1)
        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($raw)) { return $false }
        $pidVal = 0
        if (-not [int]::TryParse(([string]$raw).Trim(), [ref]$pidVal)) { return $false }
        if ($pidVal -le 0) { return $false }
        $p = Get-Process -Id $pidVal -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
        return [bool]$p
    } catch {
        return $false
    }
}

function Test-FbSplashOobeHideAllowed {
    # 5.4.5: hide OOBE/WWAHost on Audit/update boots once splash owns the screen.
    # 5.4.19: do not hide if splash is not confirmed visible, or if the WU loop
    # is not painting (skip-cascade / failed start / seal). Do not hide real
    # customer OOBE after seal / updates-done teardown.
    try {
        if ($env:FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_DISABLE_OOBE_HIDE -eq '1') { return $false }
        if ($env:FIRSTBASE_SPLASH_SUPPRESSION_DISABLE -eq '1') { return $false }
        if (Test-FbSplashSealWindowActive) { return $false }
        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSealedMarker) { return $false }
        if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $FbSplashPipelineCompletedMarker) { return $false }
        if ($script:UserPreferredTopmostOff) { return $false }
        if ($script:FbSplashOperatorGateStoodDown) { return $false }
        if ($script:Fb2241SkipWwahostMinForThisTick) { return $false }
        if (-not $script:FbSplashConfirmedVisible) { return $false }
        if (-not (Test-FbSplashWuLoopPaintingActive)) { return $false }
        if ((Test-Path -LiteralPath $Marker) -and -not (Test-FbSplash2222OobeOverlayHandoffActive)) { return $false }
        return $true
    } catch {
        return $false
    }
}

function Test-FbSplashSkipOobeHideHwnd {
    param([IntPtr]$Hwnd)
    try {
        if ($Hwnd -eq [IntPtr]::Zero) { return $true }
        if ($script:SplashNativeHwnd -ne [IntPtr]::Zero -and $Hwnd -eq $script:SplashNativeHwnd) { return $true }
        try {
            if (Get-Command Find-FbSplashYieldWindows -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) {
                foreach ($w in @(Find-FbSplashYieldWindows)) {
                    if ($w -and $w.Hwnd -eq $Hwnd) { return $true }
                }
            }
        } catch {}
        $pn = Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214cResolveProcNameFromHwnd -Hwnd $Hwnd
        $title = ''
        try { $title = Get-FbSplashWindowText -Hwnd $Hwnd } catch { $title = '' }
        if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($title)) {
            try {
                $sbT = New-Object System.Text.StringBuilder 256
                [void][FbSplashWin32Z]::GetWindowText($Hwnd, $sbT, 256)
                $title = $sbT.ToString()
            } catch { $title = '' }
        }
        if ($title -match '(?i)setting') { return $true }
        if ($title -match '(?i)(preparing your computer|getting windows ready|working on updates|configuring windows)') { return $true }
        $base = ([string]$pn) -replace '\.exe$', ''
        try {
            if (Get-Command Get-FbSplashWindowKind -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) {
                $pidU = [uint32]0
                try { [void][FbSplashWin32Z]::GetWindowThreadProcessId($Hwnd, [ref]$pidU) } catch {}
                $kind = Get-FbSplashWindowKind -ProcessName $base -Title $title -ProcessId ([int]$pidU)
                if ($kind -eq 'operator' -or $kind -eq 'console') { return $true }
            }
        } catch {}
        if ($base -match '(?i)^(SystemSettings|explorer)$') { return $true }
        return $false
    } catch {
        return $true
    }
}

function Test-FbSplashOobeChromeTitle {
    param([string]$Title)
    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($Title)) { return $false }
    # Language / keyboard / region picker and CXH "problem getting this PC ready" (Audit-on-OOBE).
    return [bool]($Title -match '(?i)(country or region|keyboard layout|language|problem getting this PC ready|Getting ready|Is this the right country)')
}

function Get-FbSplashOobeHwndTitle {
    param([IntPtr]$Hwnd)
    $title = ''
    try {
        if (Get-Command Get-FbSplashWindowText -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) {
            $title = Get-FbSplashWindowText -Hwnd $Hwnd
        }
    } catch { $title = '' }
    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($title)) {
        try {
            $sbT = New-Object System.Text.StringBuilder 512
            [void][FbSplashWin32Z]::GetWindowText($Hwnd, $sbT, 512)
            $title = $sbT.ToString()
        } catch { $title = '' }
    }
    return [string]$title
}

function Test-FbSplashIsOobeFamilyProc {
    param([string]$ProcName)
    $pn = ([string]$ProcName).ToLowerInvariant()
    if ($pn -notmatch '\.exe$') { $pn = $pn + '.exe' }
    return ($pn -eq 'applicationframehost.exe' -or $pn -eq 'cloudexperiencehost.exe' -or $pn -eq 'shellexperiencehost.exe' -or $pn -eq 'useroobebroker.exe' -or $pn -eq 'oobeldr.exe' -or $pn -eq 'wwahost.exe' -or $pn -eq 'oobe.exe')
}

function Invoke-FbSplashHideOobeHwndIfAllowed {
    param(
        [Parameter(Mandatory)][IntPtr]$Hwnd,
        [string]$ProcName = '',
        [string]$Reason = 'while-updates'
    )
    if ($Hwnd -eq [IntPtr]::Zero) { return }
    if (-not (Test-FbSplashOobeHideAllowed)) { return }
    if (Test-FbSplashSkipOobeHideHwnd -Hwnd $Hwnd) { return }
    $title = Get-FbSplashOobeHwndTitle -Hwnd $Hwnd
    $pnLower = ([string]$ProcName).ToLowerInvariant()
    if ([string]::IsNullOrWhiteSpace($pnLower)) {
        try { $pnLower = (Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214cResolveProcNameFromHwnd -Hwnd $Hwnd).ToLowerInvariant() } catch { $pnLower = '' }
    }
    $isFamily = Test-FbSplashIsOobeFamilyProc -ProcName $pnLower
    $isChrome = Test-FbSplashOobeChromeTitle -Title $title
    if (-not $isFamily -and -not $isChrome) { return }
    $key = $Hwnd.ToInt64().ToString()
    $already = $false
    try { $already = $script:OobeMin2214cHidden.ContainsKey($key) } catch { $already = $false }
    $vis = $true
    try { $vis = [FbSplashWin32Z]::IsWindowVisible($Hwnd) } catch { $vis = $true }
    if ($already -and -not $vis) { return }
    $cmd = [FbSplashWin32Z]::SW_HIDE
    $mode = 'SW_HIDE'
    if ($pnLower -eq 'wwahost.exe' -and (Test-FbSplash2227WwahostMinimizeAllowed)) {
        $cmd = [FbSplashWin32Z]::SW_MINIMIZE
        $mode = 'SW_MINIMIZE-optin'
    }
    $did = [FbSplashWin32Z]::ShowWindow($Hwnd, $cmd)
    try { $script:OobeMin2214cHidden[$key] = $pnLower } catch {}
    $visAfter = $true
    try { $visAfter = [FbSplashWin32Z]::IsWindowVisible($Hwnd) } catch {}
    if (-not $already) {
        Write-SplashLog ("5.4.20: OOBE-hide reason={0} mode={1} hwnd={2} proc={3} title={4} ShowWindow={5} visibleAfter={6}" -f $Reason, $mode, $Hwnd, $pnLower, $title, $did, $visAfter)
        return
    }
    $now = [datetime]::UtcNow
    $last = $null
    try { $last = $script:OobeHideReassertUtc[$key] } catch {}
    if ($null -eq $last -or ($now - $last).TotalSeconds -ge 30) {
        try { $script:OobeHideReassertUtc[$key] = $now } catch {}
        Write-SplashLog ("5.4.20: OOBE-hide-reassert reason={0} hwnd={1} proc={2} title={3} visibleBefore={4} ShowWindow={5} visibleAfter={6}" -f $Reason, $Hwnd, $pnLower, $title, $vis, $did, $visAfter)
    }
}

function Invoke-FbSplash2228OverlayEarlyZOrderPass {
    param([string]$Reason = 'unspecified')
    try {
        if (-not (Test-FbSplash2227OobeOverlayPipelineActive)) { return }
        if ($script:SplashNativeHwnd -eq [IntPtr]::Zero) { return }
        if ($script:UserPreferredTopmostOff) { return }
        Write-SplashLog ("2229: overlay early Z-order pass ({0}) - 2214l + WWAHost SW_MINIMIZE when pipeline active (DISABLE_WWAHOST_MINIMIZE=1 opts out)" -f $Reason) 'INFO'
        $yieldEarly = $false
        try { $yieldEarly = [bool](Invoke-FbSplashHonorOperatorForeground) } catch { $yieldEarly = $false }
        if (-not $yieldEarly) {
            $window.Topmost = $true
            Invoke-FbSplashApplyWin32ZOrder -WantTopmost $true
        }
        Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214lPlaceWwahostRootBehindSplash -RestackPass 1
        if ($yieldEarly) {
            try { Invoke-FbSplashHonorOperatorForeground | Out-Null } catch {}
        } else {
            [void]$window.Activate()
            Invoke-FbSplashMaybeReclaimForegroundFromOobe
        }
        Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214lPlaceWwahostRootBehindSplash -RestackPass 2
        # 2214l-enum: enumerate all visible WWAHost roots without fg gate; no throttle on the one-time early Z-pass.
        Invoke-FbSplashOobe2214lEnumerateAndPlaceAllWwahostBehindSplash -NoThrottle
        if ($yieldEarly) {
            try { Invoke-FbSplashHonorOperatorForeground | Out-Null } catch {}
        }
    } catch {
        Write-SplashLog ("2228: overlay early Z-order pass EXCEPTION ({0}): {1}" -f $Reason, $_.Exception.Message) 'WARN'
    }
}
$StatusFile = Join-Path $FbRoot 'wu-status.json'
# 2221: true while splash holds open for overlay handoff UI (marker + overlay file both present).
$script:Splash2218DeferCloseForOobeOverlay = $false
# 2214c: HWND keys (Int64 string) -> process name at hide time; restore drains this map.
